# Non-English and non-ASCII traffic.
# Rules written against ASCII payloads tend to treat anything else as suspicious
# encoding. Multi-byte UTF-8 percent-encodes into long %XX runs that look like
# obfuscation, and normalisation forms that differ byte-wise are the same word to
# a human. Refusing these locks out entire markets, which is the most expensive
# false positive a gateway can produce.
